INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S COTTAGE - HOMEOWNERS ASSOCIATION MEETING - NIGHT

A cramped round room. Folding chairs in a circle. A banner reads "COASTLINE ESTATES HOA - TOGETHER WE'RE SAFE." A tray of lemon bars sits under cling film.

BEATRIZ, 50s, board president, bangs a gavel made from a baseball bat. DWIGHT, 40s, treasurer, shuffles receipts. KOFI, 30s, a new resident, holds a clipboard he didn't ask for. MARISOL, 60s, the neighborhood gossip, sits with her arms crossed. ARNOLD "BIG A" TREMBLAY, 70, a retired harbor pilot, eats lemon bars.

BEATRIZ
Order. Order! First item. The lighthouse.

DWIGHT
What about it?

BEATRIZ
It's a lighthouse.

DWIGHT
We know that.

BEATRIZ
It's lit.

KOFI
Isn't that the point?

MARISOL
It shines in my kitchen.

BEATRIZ
Marisol, it shines in everyone's kitchen.

MARISOL
Yes, but it shines in mine.

BIG A
I like it.

BEATRIZ
Arnold, you aren't on the agenda.

BIG A
I'm on the cake.

DWIGHT
Lemon bars aren't cake.

BIG A
I'm on the lemon bars.

KOFI
Can I add something?

BEATRIZ
No.

KOFI
Okay, but I measured the beam.

MARISOL
You measured it?

KOFI
Forty-one seconds between sweeps.

DWIGHT
It's supposed to be thirty.

BEATRIZ
It is thirty.

KOFI
It's forty-one.

BEATRIZ
It's thirty!

BIG A
It's forty-one. I piloted that channel for twenty-two years.

MARISOL
You? You weren't even there for the vote.

BIG A
I was at the cake.

DWIGHT
It's not cake!

Beatriz bangs the bat-gavel on the arm of her chair. The cling film jumps.

BEATRIZ
Motion to table the lighthouse until we can agree on the time!

DWIGHT
Seconded!

MARISOL
Opposed!

KOFI
Opposed!

BIG A
Who's counting?

BEATRIZ
I'm counting!

KOFI
Then why is it forty-one?

BEATRIZ
It's thirty!

The lighthouse beam sweeps across the room's curved window, throwing a white bar over their faces. They all freeze, counting under their breath.

BEATRIZ (CONT'D)
(whispering)
Thirty-one... thirty-two...

DWIGHT
(whispering)
Thirty-eight...

KOFI
(whispering)
Forty.

BIG A
Forty-one.

The beam sweeps again. A long, silent beat. Beatriz sets the bat down very gently.

BEATRIZ
Motion to table the clock.

DWIGHT
Seconded.

MARISOL
Fine. I'll take a lemon bar.

BIG A
There aren't any.
